{"id": "2026-11-12-news-us-envoys-meet-putin-after-abu-dhabi-talks", "date": "2026-11-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "US envoys meet Putin after Abu Dhabi talks", "summary": "Kushner and Witkoff met Putin in Moscow on 12 November after Abu Dhabi trilateral talks ended with a 1,000-plus prisoner swap deal but no breakthrough.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/international/verhandlungen-zu-ukraine-krieg-die-gespraeche-in-abu-dhabi-sind-beendet-so-geht-es-weiter", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "US envoys Jared Kushner and Steve Witkoff arrived in Moscow on Thursday 12 November to meet Vladimir Putin, a day after the first US-mediated direct talks between Russia and Ukraine since February ended in Abu Dhabi with a prisoner-exchange deal but no breakthrough on ending the war. The two days of trilateral talks closed on Wednesday 11 November. Russia's TASS news agency, citing Lieutenant General Alexander Sorin, reported that each side will exchange more than 1,000 prisoners within the next two to three weeks. Positions on territory remain far apart: Russia, which controls about a fifth of Ukraine, wants Kyiv to give up the whole Donbas region, and President Volodymyr Zelensky rejects any cession of land. Ukraine's negotiator David Arakhamia called the talks \"hard\" and said a solution \"before the new year\" was possible; Kushner called them \"a good first step\". After Moscow, the envoys are due to meet Zelensky in Dublin on Friday 13 November, where more than 40 European leaders are meeting today at the European Political Community summit. Russia's chief negotiator Vladimir Medinsky said the Russian side had no contact with the European officials present in Abu Dhabi.", "why": "a prisoner swap of this size is the only concrete result so far, and the next step depends on whether Putin accepts Europeans at the table, which Washington and Kyiv want and Moscow has refused.", "thread_id": "2026-11-12-news-us-envoys-meet-putin-after-abu-dhabi-talks", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-12", "event_date": "2026-11-12", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Russia", "Ukraine", "Vladimir Putin", "Steve Witkoff", "Jared Kushner"]}
{"id": "2026-11-12-news-israel-readies-military-for-possible-iran-strike", "date": "2026-11-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "Israel readies military for possible Iran strike", "summary": "KAN reported Israel's security cabinet ordered the military to step up preparations for a possible attack on Iran; Iran threatened bases from West Asia to Europe.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/12/iran-warns-of-expanded-retaliation-as-israel-reportedly-readies-to-attack", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Israel's security cabinet, chaired by caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, ordered the military to step up preparations for a possible attack on Iran, the public broadcaster KAN reported on the evening of Wednesday 11 November. KAN said the directives \"could lead it to carry out activities that could trigger a war\". They became public after opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot, whom President Isaac Herzog asked to form a government after Netanyahu's coalition lost its majority in the October election, told Netanyahu not to use the military \"without a direct and immediate threat\" until a new government is in place. Iran's security chief Mohsen Rezaei replied that every base used in an attack, \"from West Asia to Europe\", would be a target. The reports come while Qatar is trying to broker a US–Iran deal. KAN's report has not been confirmed by the Israeli government.", "why": "a government with no majority would be preparing a possible new war while its likely successor objects, and Iran's threat now explicitly covers bases in Europe.", "thread_id": "2026-11-12-news-israel-readies-military-for-possible-iran-strike", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-12", "event_date": "2026-11-11", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Israel", "Iran", "Benjamin Netanyahu", "Gadi Eisenkot"]}
{"id": "2026-11-12-news-democrat-colom-wins-mississippi-senate-seat", "date": "2026-11-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "Democrat Colom wins Mississippi Senate seat", "summary": "AP projected Democrat Scott Colom defeated Senator Cindy Hyde-Smith in Mississippi, the state's first Black senator since Reconstruction.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/mississippi-senate-race-democrat-scott-colom-defeats-republican-cindy-hyde-smith/a-79924938", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Democrat Scott Colom defeated Republican Senator Cindy Hyde-Smith in Mississippi, the Associated Press projected on Wednesday 11 November, after more than a week of counting from the 3 November midterm election. Colom, 43, becomes the state's first Black US senator since Reconstruction and the first new Democratic senator Mississippi has elected since 1947. According to DW, the result gives Democrats 55 of the Senate's 100 seats, with Alaska still undecided. Democrats also won the House of Representatives.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-12-news-democrat-colom-wins-mississippi-senate-seat", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-12", "event_date": "2026-11-11", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Scott Colom", "Cindy Hyde-Smith", "Mississippi", "US Senate"]}
{"id": "2026-11-12-news-indonesia-s-vice-president-gibran-resigns", "date": "2026-11-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "Indonesia's vice president Gibran resigns", "summary": "Indonesian Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka resigned after courts ruled his education documents did not meet election requirements.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/12/indonesia-vice-president-resigns-amid-dispute-over-eligibility", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Indonesia's Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka, the eldest son of former President Joko Widodo, resigned on Thursday 12 November after courts ruled that the documents he submitted on his schooling abroad did not meet election requirements. President Prabowo Subianto said he accepted the resignation \"with a heavy heart\". Last month the Constitutional Court and the Supreme Court found the education documents insufficient; critics say he never received a high-school diploma. Gibran, 39, served two years of a five-year term. Under the constitution there is no new election: Prabowo nominates two candidates and the People's Consultative Assembly elects one within 60 days.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-12-news-indonesia-s-vice-president-gibran-resigns", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-12", "event_date": "2026-11-12", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Indonesia", "Gibran Rakabuming Raka", "Prabowo Subianto"]}
{"id": "2026-11-12-news-russia-s-ambassador-to-the-us-dies", "date": "2026-11-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "Russia's ambassador to the US dies", "summary": "Russia's Foreign Ministry said ambassador to the US Alexander Darchiev died of a chronic illness aged 66.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/monde/l-ambassadeur-russe-aux-etats-unis-est-mort-soudainement", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Alexander Darchiev, Russia's ambassador to the United States, has died in Moscow aged 66 of a chronic illness, the Russian Foreign Ministry announced on Wednesday 11 November. Putin appointed him in March 2025, after Donald Trump returned to the White House. Ministry spokeswoman Maria Zakharova warned against \"conspiracy theories\" about his death. His death leaves the post empty while Washington and Moscow are negotiating over Ukraine.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-12-news-russia-s-ambassador-to-the-us-dies", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-12", "event_date": "2026-11-11", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Alexander Darchiev", "Russia", "United States"]}
{"id": "2026-11-12-news-finance-department-fines-ex-cs-chair-rohner", "date": "2026-11-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "Finance department fines ex-CS chair Rohner", "summary": "The Federal Department of Finance fined former Credit Suisse chairman Urs Rohner for false information to FINMA over the spying affair; he has asked for a court ruling.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/wirtschaft/cs-beschattungsaffaere-credit-suisse-bund-buesst-ex-praesident-urs-rohner", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The Federal Department of Finance has fined former Credit Suisse chairman Urs Rohner for deliberately giving false information to the financial regulator FINMA about the bank's 2019 spying affair, SRF Investigativ and Republik reported on Thursday 12 November. The penalty order, dated 20 October and not yet final, sets a suspended fine of 144 daily rates of CHF 690 and a fine of CHF 24,840. The offence carries up to three years in prison. When FINMA asked in 2019, the bank called the surveillance of former manager Iqbal Khan an \"isolated event\". The department found that seven surveillance operations were planned or carried out between 2016 and 2019, and that a complaint about then-CEO Tidjane Thiam was not reported. It finds Rohner mostly negligent, but deliberate in two cases. Rohner rejects all the accusations \"fully and firmly\" and has asked for a court ruling, so the case now goes to the Federal Criminal Court in Bellinzona. He is presumed innocent.", "why": "the court's ruling will test whether the chair of a systemically important bank answers personally for what the bank tells its supervisor.", "thread_id": "2026-11-12-news-finance-department-fines-ex-cs-chair-rohner", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-12", "event_date": "2026-10-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Urs Rohner", "Credit Suisse", "FINMA", "Federal Department of Finance"]}
{"id": "2026-11-12-news-swiss-raids-target-cocaine-shipping-network", "date": "2026-11-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss raids target cocaine shipping network", "summary": "Federal prosecutors and fedpol searched 84 sites and detained 41 people in Switzerland in an international operation against a cocaine-smuggling and laundering network.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/kqFmoxC7Mw7M", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Swiss federal prosecutors and fedpol searched 84 sites and detained 41 people in Switzerland on 10–11 November in an international operation against a suspected network that smuggled cocaine from Latin America to Europe, they announced on Thursday 12 November. The suspected network, active since at least early 2019, hid cocaine in shipping containers of legal goods sent to shell trading companies registered in Switzerland and the Netherlands. Police acted in 12 cantons and seven other countries. Prosecutors are seeking pre-trial detention for five people, three others are held abroad pending extradition, and more than CHF 2.3 million, CHF 50,000 in crypto-assets and 15 weapons were seized. A shipment of more than 750 kg was intercepted in Antwerp in August.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-12-news-swiss-raids-target-cocaine-shipping-network", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-12", "event_date": "2026-11-11", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["fedpol", "Office of the Attorney General of Switzerland", "Europol"]}
{"id": "2026-11-12-news-swiss-ilo-unemployment-rises-to-5-6", "date": "2026-11-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss ILO unemployment rises to 5.6%", "summary": "The Federal Statistical Office's labour force survey put ILO unemployment at 5.6% in Q3 2026, up from 5.1% a year earlier.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/CXwrzhzqrnVn", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Switzerland's unemployment rate by the international ILO definition rose to 5.6% in the third quarter of 2026, from 5.1% a year earlier, the Federal Statistical Office reported on Thursday 12 November. This survey count is higher than SECO's registered-unemployment rate because it also includes jobseekers not registered with a job centre. 288,000 people were unemployed, 27,000 more than a year ago. Employment grew 0.5% year on year, but only 0.1% in full-time equivalents, and fell 0.3% from the second quarter after seasonal adjustment. Unemployment also rose in neighbouring countries: France reached 8.4%, Italy 6.5%, Austria 6.1% and Germany 4.2%.", "why": "the quarterly drop in jobs and the near-flat full-time count show the labour market cooling faster than the annual headcount suggests.", "thread_id": "2026-11-12-news-swiss-ilo-unemployment-rises-to-5-6", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-12", "event_date": "2026-11-12", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Statistical Office", "Switzerland"]}
{"id": "2026-11-12-news-hearing-aid-allowances-rise-10-percent", "date": "2026-11-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "Hearing-aid allowances rise 10 percent", "summary": "AHV and IV flat-rate allowances for adult hearing aids rise 10% from 1 January 2027.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/r2uYAGMJxRiK", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland", "health"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The flat-rate amounts that old-age (AHV/AVS) and disability (IV/AI) insurance pay for adults' hearing aids will rise by 10% from 1 January 2027, the Federal Council announced on Thursday 12 November. Repair allowances and the maximum amounts for children's hearing aids paid by disability insurance are also being adjusted.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-12-news-hearing-aid-allowances-rise-10-percent", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-12", "event_date": "2026-11-12", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["AHV", "IV", "Federal Council"]}
